/**
 * A SimExprSimpleNode is a node in a SimExpr expression tree.
 * A reference to the root node is obtained with SimExpr.getRoot().
 * The SimExpr constructors parse the input expression and call
 * a number of SimExprSimpleNode methods on the root node after the parse.
 * Firstly, trim() is called to remove redundant nodes from the tree.
 * A node is redundant where it contains no token and has a single child:
 * it is replaced with the child node. Secondly, resolve() is called to
 * resolve references to threepl identifiers (clocks and variables) and
 * generate values for constant and literal nodes. Thirdly, getType()
 * is called to type check the expression and generate storage for
 * node values where these have not already been created in resolve().
 * Finally, compressLiteral() is called to replace node sub-trees consisting
 * purely of literal or constant nodes with a single literal node.
 *
 * Once the above process has successfully completed, the expression
 * may be evaluated with the eval() method. eval() returns a SimExpNodeValue
 * object which contains the expression result. Refer SimExpNodeValue
 * for methods to access the value. The expr() method may be called to
 * return the expression String. This will be different to the originally
 * parsed expression String if any literals were removed in compressLiteral().
 * 
 * @version $Revision: 8254 $
 * @author Generated by JJTree, modified Andrew Tulloh
 */
